[ti:One]
[ar:Birdtalker]

[00:02.56] 
[00:13.68] I've played the teacher, the preacher, guru
[00:18.25] Maintaining postures separating me and you
[00:23.23] As if the thoughts of God were mine and mine to speak
[00:31.53] I've listened with an agenda so I could prove
[00:36.84] All of the shit I believe to be true
[00:40.74] Just to hide the fear of being weak
[00:49.38] Burn the scorecards, balance out the scales
[00:54.53] We are one wind distracted by our different sails
[01:02.90] Underneath what's detectable with eyes
[01:07.96] Every particle's vibrating with the same life
[01:13.01] 
[01:24.71] If we keep running around deciding who's right and wrong
[01:29.12] Then tell me, where are we headed?
[01:31.64] How can we all belong
[01:33.76] When all our logic is colliding
[01:36.37] And it's constantly dividing me from you
[01:43.18] So damn those eager protestations on your tongue
[01:48.48] Shut your brain up long enough to hear the lowly hum
[01:56.92] Underneath what's detectable with eyes
[02:01.81] Every particle's vibrating with the one life
[02:07.46] 
[02:37.97] Beyond the land of the right, the land of the wrong
[02:45.47] There's a field waiting for us
[02:48.90] All the notions of you, the notions of me
[02:53.80] We finally agree don't mean a thing
